home=profile+tabs+f'''<div class="dashboard" id="profile-overview"><div class="stack"><section class="card"><div class="card-heading"><h2>About me</h2><span>THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORK</span></div><h2 class="intro-title">Understanding the attack.<br><em>Improving the defence.</em></h2><p class="intro-copy">I’m Joseph, an infrastructure and cybersecurity professional and Co-founder &amp; Head of Operations and Cybersecurity at RedShoulder.</p><p class="intro-copy">Belisarius is my personal space for exploring Azure and Windows security through practical Purple Teaming: testing assumptions, examining telemetry, and turning findings into better defences.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Security operations</span><span class="tag">Incident response</span><span class="tag">Cloud security</span></div>{link('about.html','More about my background')}<div class="role-line"><span class="role-icon">R</span><div><strong>Co-founder · Operations &amp; Cybersecurity</strong><small>RedShoulder · <a href="https://redshoulder.co.za/">Visit company ↗</a></small></div></div></section><section class="card"><div class="card-heading"><h2>How I approach security</h2><span>THE PURPLE TEAM CYCLE</span></div><p class="intro-copy">A finding becomes useful when we can explain what happened, what the defender saw, and whether the improvement holds up to another test.</p>{method}{link('projects.html','Explore the research roadmap')}</section></div><div class="stack"><section class="card" id="focus"><div class="card-heading"><h2>Areas of focus</h2><span>01 — 03</span></div>{focus}</section><section class="card" id="social"><div class="card-heading"><h2>Find me online</h2><span>JOIN THE CONVERSATION</span></div>{socials()}</section><section class="card"><span class="eyebrow">OPEN TO CONNECTIONS</span><h3>Good security starts<br>with a conversation.</h3><p class="intro-copy">Employment opportunities, consulting enquiries, and technical collaboration.</p>{link('contact.html','Get in touch')}</section></div></div><div class="section-head" id="up-next"><div><span class="eyebrow">BUILDING IN THE OPEN</span><h2>What’s coming next</h2></div><span class="muted">The first lab studies are being planned.</span></div>{project_cards()}'''
about=heading('BACKGROUND & APPROACH','The person behind Belisarius.','Infrastructure, security operations, and a focus on making defensive improvements practical.')+f'''<div class="dashboard"><div class="stack"><section class="card"><h2>Joseph Taomhera</h2><p>I bring experience across infrastructure support, SOC operations, incident response, and technical leadership. I am Co-founder and Head of Operations and Cybersecurity at RedShoulder.</p><p>My personal focus is Azure and Windows security. Through Belisarius, I’m building a body of practical research around identity, endpoint visibility, detection engineering, and defensive validation.</p><p>I’m based in Cape Town, South Africa, and welcome international employment opportunities, consulting enquiries, and collaboration with security practitioners.</p>{link('assets/joseph-taomhera-cv.pdf','Download my CV','button secondary','download')}</section><section class="card"><div class="card-heading"><h2>Experience</h2><span>SELECTED BACKGROUND</span></div><ul class="timeline"><li><strong>Co-founder · Head of Operations &amp; Cybersecurity</strong><span>RedShoulder · Current leadership role</span><p>Operations and cybersecurity leadership.</p></li><li><strong>NOC / SOC Engineer</strong><span>BDR Group · 2025–present, as listed in CV</span><p>Network and security monitoring, alert triage, threat hunting, and incident response.</p></li><li><strong>Senior IT Specialist</strong><span>121 BPO Client Services · 2024–2025</span><p>Infrastructure support, technical projects, and ISO 27001:2022 implementation work.</p></li><li><strong>Cyber Security Analyst</strong><span>RedShoulder · 2020–2024</span><p>Security event monitoring, incident investigation, and threat analysis.</p></li><li><strong>Service Desk Team Lead</strong><span>Sharaf Shipping · 2017–2020</span><p>Technical support leadership, escalation management, and infrastructure operations.</p></li></ul></section></div><div class="stack"><section class="card"><div class="card-heading"><h2>Credentials</h2><span>AS LISTED IN MY CV</span></div><div class="credentials">{''.join(f'<div class="credential"><strong>{name}</strong><span>{desc}</span></div>' for name,desc in [('Microsoft Security','SC-100 · SC-200 · AZ-500 · Security fundamentals'),('Google Cloud','Cloud Security Engineer'),('EC-Council','Certified SOC Analyst'),('CompTIA','Security+'),('UniAthena','Diploma in Business Administration')])}</div></section><section class="card"><h2>Why publish?</h2><p>To make the reasoning visible: the scenario, the evidence, the uncertainty, and the change that improved the outcome.</p><p>I value useful explanations and reproducible work that other practitioners can question, test, and improve.</p>{link('research.html','Explore the writing')}</section></div></div>'''
